course: dictionary
lesson: 1685
title: Christianity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Christianity is a religion. A religion is a set of beliefs about God and how people should live. Christianity is based on the life and teaching of Jesus Christ, so Jesus is at the heart of it.
explain: The context tells you more. «Christianity is the largest world religion, with about a third of the world's people.» Largest and a third of the world's people are clues that Christianity is a very big religion followed by many people.
explain: Christians believe Jesus is the Son of God, who died and rose again, and they follow the Bible. The word can also mean all the Christian people and churches together, as in «Christianity grew slowly over generations».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Christianity became the official religion of the Roman Empire» still make sense if you read it as a religion based on the teaching of Jesus? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: A religion is a set of beliefs about God or gods and how people should live.
fact: «Christianity» is the religion based on the life and teaching of Jesus Christ.
fact: Christians follow the Bible and believe Jesus is the Son of God, who died and rose again.
fact: «Christianity» can also mean Christian people and churches as a whole.
fact: «Christianity is the largest world religion, with about a third of the world's people.»
exercise: «Christianity is the largest world religion, with about a third of the world's people.» What is Christianity? | A type of music from Byzantium | A school subject about maths | *A religion based on the life and teaching of Jesus Christ
exercise: «Jesus was Jewish, and Christianity grew out of Judaism.» What does this sentence tell you? | Christianity is a river in Kyiv | Judaism is a kind of festival | Jesus was Christian | *Jesus was Jewish, and Christianity came from Judaism
exercise: «Around 988 Prince Volodymyr of Kyiv took Christianity from Byzantium.» Where did Volodymyr take Christianity from? | Rome | *Byzantium | Kyiv | Dnipro
test: What do Christians believe about Jesus? | He was a prince of Kyiv | *He is the Son of God, who died and rose again | He lived in Rome as a king | He was a farmer
test: What book do Christians follow? | Byzantium | The official book of Rome | The Dnipro | *The Bible
exam: Besides the religion itself, what else can the word Christianity mean? | A Roman coin | A festival held in Kyiv | A river where people were baptised | *Christian people and churches as a whole
